Track 1: Unstamped Envelope Drifted Past the Air Lock
- Story & Context: In the dark corridors of Sector 4, teenage deckhand Arlo intercepted a physical letter dropped by an engineer into an unmonitored waste chute, its wax seal cracked and address smeared into unintelligible star-coords. The song opens with a screeching 210 BPM skate-punk riff that suddenly drops out, leaving only Arlo’s breathing and a eerie, 12-bar music box loop echoing against the steel hull. As the gang vocals kick in, the band recreates the terror of watching a piece of personal history float away into the black vacuum. "We sent our love by carrier signal, but the outer hull just ate the ink!"
